<h1>ContHunt for agents</h1>
<p class="docs-lede">Connect ContHunt to your coding agent so it can find and analyze viral TikToks, Reels, and Shorts on your account.</p>

<dl class="docs-meta">
    <div>
        <dt>MCP</dt>
        <dd>https://mcp.conthunt.app</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
        <dt>Skill</dt>
        <dd>npx skills add https://conthunt.app</dd>
    </div>
</dl>

<div class="docs-cards">
    <a class="docs-card" href="/docs/integrations/mcp">
        <h2>MCP</h2>
        <p>The live connection. Your agent signs into ContHunt and can search, analyze, and research from chat.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="docs-card" href="/docs/integrations/skill">
        <h2>Skill</h2>
        <p>A short playbook the agent reads so it already knows when and how to use ContHunt for social content research.</p>
    </a>
</div>

<h2>Which one do you need?</h2>
<p>MCP is the connection. After you add it, the agent can actually run ContHunt on your account.</p>
<p>The skill is optional. It does not connect anything by itself. It tells the agent what ContHunt is and how to use it, so you do not have to explain the product every time.</p>
<p>Most people add MCP first, then the skill.</p>

<h2>Tell the agent</h2>
<p>If you would rather paste a sentence than run a command:</p>
<div class="docs-code">
    <button type="button" class="docs-copy" data-copy>Copy</button>
